BridgeDock browser-login adaptation (2026-11-03)
----------------------------------------------
The bundled library includes the local CursorWebLogin.patch, based on
cursor-agent2api v0.2.2, commit 75a9770b06f6eeba3f1cdd8da12a7a9fa5c8987d.
It adds Grok Bot proof-key browser login, polling, credential persistence,
Cursor refresh-token renewal and selected-team request headers.
Rebuild with Vendor/build-cursor-web-login.sh.

Protocol references:
https://github.com/qunqin24/Pulse/blob/main/Sources/Pulse/Auth/CursorWebLogin.swift
https://github.com/andreanjos/grokbot-headless/blob/main/grok-bot-headless.mjs
The flow and renewal endpoint were also checked against the installed
Grok Bot 0.78.1 application. The adaptation does not embed personal credentials.

BridgeDock session import adaptation (2026-11-04)
-----------------------------------------------
CursorSessionLogin.patch adds explicitly imported Cursor web sessions to the
Agent v1 transport. Session identity is checked at cursor.com/api/auth/me.
Unlike API keys and browser OAuth refresh tokens, pasted sessions cannot renew
themselves: their original expiry is retained and re-import is required then.
The patch preserves existing API-key and Grok Bot login behavior.
It also supplies per-account execution scopes and per-request session IDs,
discovers exact Agent model IDs through GetUsableModels, keeps structured
Cursor error reasons, and treats cancellation of unrelated native execs as a
per-exec notification rather than failure of the entire model response.
The advertised CLI build matches the official installer checked on 2026-11-04:
cli-2026.10.22-27dcf5f. Max-mode-only catalog entries are not advertised.
Protocol references: https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi (MIT) and
https://cursor.com/install. No source from these references is bundled.

BridgeDock MCP catalog compatibility (2026-11-04)
-----------------------------------------------
CursorToolCatalog.patch adds the server-managed MCP catalog lookup allowlist,
McpStateExecArgs responses using the caller's advertised tools, and support
for catalog and tool-count transcript notifications in Cursor 3.27.22.
Specific regression tests cover catalog filtering, request IDs, notification
handling, and continued rejection of unknown protocol fields.
Protocol references include the installed Cursor 3.27.22 descriptors and
https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/main/packages/ai/src/providers/cursor/exec-modern.ts
(MIT). The local adaptation reuses the existing wire encoder.
